One of the nice features of tunneling dwarves is they leave behind a
ready supply of the rocks that can be used to kill them.  But even
better is the fact that they tend to appear a level deeper than the
gnomes who supply so many early daggers and daggers work much better
than rocks.

A fighter class like valk, knight etc can just be at full hit points and
melee a lone dwarf to death.  That's a bad idea for classes who start
with worse weapons and armor.

This same principle applies to getting that first silver saber.  The one
who has a chance of carrying one is much stronger.  I've lost a lot of
pets to the one carrying a silver saber in the mines.


